From f4cba74560a255702cd8f3d5999bb0ead4da867f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:11:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! Fog: Wind Waker HD's curve, the square of the
 GameCube's linear fog, while the host has HD's distances in place

Wind Waker HD mixes its fog in linear light: its scenery shader ends with
mix(lit, fog colour, f), both linear, and the frame goes out through an
sRGB output. GX mixes in the game's gamma, so a dark wall deep in a
room's fog kept half of HD's fog or less. Read from the captures:
GanonB far wall at 6561 units, f 0.682, HD red 0.229 where a gamma mix
gives 0.169; Tower of the Gods at 6024 units, f 0.609, HD 0.099 against
0.047.

With HD's curve, the draws' fog (emit_fog and the ubershader) is now
that mix in linear light by the sRGB curve, in place of the integer
blend. The sun pass reads the scene from a copy taken just before it
(the frame buffer only, single-sampled). On the lit scenery it takes
the draws' fog out in linear light, shades as before, and puts HD's
radial fog back in linear light. Without the copy it works as before.

Far half of the dungeon stops against Cemu, linear luminance before ->
after (Cemu): Forbidden Woods R05 0.056 -> 0.065 (0.064), with its hue
back from orange; Earth Temple R00 0.027 -> 0.039 (0.037); Wind Temple
R02 0.059 -> 0.074 (0.073); GanonB 0.110 -> 0.118 (0.123).
